        "comments": "The assembly mMusErm2.hap2.1 is based on 27x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. This genome has been assembled using PacBio and HiC data and phased. The result is two curated haplotypes. The X and Y chromosome was identified by copy number in assembly. Multiple rearrangements (inversions, translocations) was observed in the region on chromosome 10 (92.9-113.2 Mbp). The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome X (78.3 - 86.9 Mbp) are unknown. A large number of repeats is in the unlocalised sequences.",
